Vendored inside a package, and not covered by that package's own licence
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Eigen                  MPL-2.0. Not a dependency of this project and not chosen by it:
                           Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime compiles Eigen into its native runtime,
                           and says so in its own ThirdPartyNotices.txt. The package's nuspec
                           declares MIT, which is true of the package's own code and does not
                           reach this. Recorded here because a licence file that names one
                           licence is not a statement about everything shipped beside it.

                           ONNX Runtime 1.29.0 pins Eigen by commit, so the commit is what
                           identifies what was compiled in:

                             1d8b82b0740839c0de7f1242a3585e3390ff5f33
                             https://gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen

                           MPL-2.0 is file-scope copyleft and its section 3.3 permits a Larger
                           Work under other terms, so this obliges attribution and a pointer to
                           the source rather than anything about d47's own licence. ONNX Runtime
                           also compiles with -DEIGEN_MPL2_ONLY unconditionally, which excludes
                           the LGPL corner of Eigen.

    OpenPhonemizer         BSD-3-Clause-Clear, over DeepPhonemizer (MIT). Only its pronunciation
    dictionary             dictionary is used and it is downloaded rather than shipped; the
                           neural model in the same repository is not used at all, having
                           measured 0.0% exact on words from its own training set.

    Kokoro-82M             Apache-2.0, hosted by onnx-community. The model and its voice files
                           are downloaded on request rather than shipped, the same way the
                           speech-to-text models are.


